task: cbor-skip-threshold-trampoline
agent: opus-depth
started: 2026-09-10
branch: feature/cbor-skip-threshold-trampoline
worktree: ../okay-wt-cbor-skip
spec: specs/iterative-recursive-decode.md (target 4: Cbor.In.skipItem)

why: Cbor.In.skipItem skips an undeclared field's value recursively —
  a tag (major 6) recurses via skipItem() again, an array/map (major
  4/5) recurses via many()->skipItem() per element. Uniformly typed
  (Either[String, Unit]), so no cross-type R-threading is needed —
  simpler than either closed root.

what: the SAME enter/leave counter already gates skipItem for
  Codecs.maxDepth's refusal (unchanged); add the native/Cont.defer
  split at the SAME NativeThreshold Cbor.get already uses (shared
  constant, one number for the whole reader), via a Cont-based
  skipItemC mirroring skipItem's own major-type dispatch.

predict: a chain of undeclared, deeply nested fields decodes/skips
  without native stack cost past the threshold; the common case (a
  shallow unknown field, or none) shows no JMH regression at 3 forks.
